I've been collecting notes on good typesetting style for Lojban:

  http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=typography

One of the open questions related to the fact that we allow 1, 2, 3,
&c to mean pa, re, ci, &c.  Since we do this, how should we treat
123.5?  What about 1,024?  '.' and ',' are both valid lerfu, so is
it ambiguous to write "1,234.56"?  camxes parses this, but drops the
decimal point.  ;-)  (I'm ignoring the issue also that these are
not universal conventions for writing numbers)

Then do you want to allow 1:23:59 to mean 1 hour, 23 minutes, 59
seconds?  Can you pronounce ':' pi'e?

These seem to be natural questions that arise from allowing 1 => pa.
I think your too clever by half example is a great contribution to
this question.

-Alan

